===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlʌstə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-lustre.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌstə|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewk-}}
From {{der|en|frm|lustre}}. See {{m|en|luster}} (etymology 1).

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|British spelling}} {{alternative form of|en|luster}} (shine, etc.)
# {{lb|en|geology}} The way in which the [[surface]] of any particular type of [[mineral]] reflects light differently from other minerals, which is helpful in telling minerals apart.
#: {{ux|en|Various kinds of minerals differ in their '''lustre'''; iron pyrites are described as having a [[metallic]] '''lustre''', glassy materials a [[vitreous]] '''lustre'''; others, such as opal, look [[resinous]], and the '''lustres''' of yet others are described as being either pearly, or silky, or dull, like earth.}}
# A glass ornament such as a [[prism]] or [[cut glass]] dangling beneath a [[chandelier]]; usually in [[cluster]]s or [[festoon]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Shena Mackay|title=Redhill Rococo|passage=...he went out through the unfamiliar hall, setting the [[chandelier]] [[clash]]ing its dusty '''lustres''' with his hand, leaving a [[prismatic]] [[jangle]] behind him in the empty house.|isbn=978-1-4481-8981-6}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[chandelier]], particularly one [[decorate]]d with glass lustres.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1838|author=John Henry Brady|title=A new pocket guide to London and its [[environs]]|passage=In the centre is painted an eagle, from whose beak an [[elegant]] glass '''lustre''' chandelier is [[suspend]]ed. There are also ten smaller chandeliers in different parts of the room.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=8g8HAAAAQAAJ}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1889|author=Anonymous|title=The Journal of Gas Lighting, Water Supply & Sanitary Improvement|passage=On the ground floor, the library (a room in carved oak) is lighted by a '''lustre''' composed of twelve [[regenerative]] burners enclosed in [[tint]]ed glasses.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=rNVHAQAAMAAJ}}

