==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
From either {{bor|es|fr|lustre}} or {{bor|es|ca|llustre}}, from {{der|es|it|lustro}}, derived from the verb {{m|it|lustrare}}. A French or Catalan intermediate is likely due to the change in the final vowel, typical of borrowings that are ultimately early Italianisms before the 16th century. Not attested in Old Spanish; first attested in [[w:Antonio de Nebrija|Nebrija]].

====Noun====
{{es-noun|m}}

# {{l|en|lustre}}, [[shine]]
#: {{ux|es|el '''lustre''' de mis zapatos, del metal, de los minerales|the '''shine''' of my shoes, of the metal, of minerals}}
#* {{Q|es|Antonio de Nebrija|Vocabulario español-latino|year=1495|quote=Blanquear dando '''lustre'''. ''candifico .as.''|t=To whiten giving '''lustre''': {{m|la|candifico|candificō, -ās}}.}}

